description:
GOAL: prove the L1->L6 architecture integrates end-to-end AND the perf story holds, BEFORE farming the layer epics — the single de-risking gate (spine doc sec 11; sec 1 'tracer'). This is THROWAWAY scaffolding that validates the SHAPE, not production code.

SCOPE — a minimal vertical slice for ONE tiny construct (an integer + binary expression like 1+2):
1. Parse it with a tiny hand-written RD routine in the grammar-DSL style (doc Layer 4 / GRAMMAR_DSL.md) into
2. a new-style PER-TYPE ARENA node carrying a typed id (ExprId) + a byte-offset span in a side-table (doc Layer 1 / sec 10.E);
3. run ONE memoized query over it ('type of node N') through a minimal red-green memo store (doc Layer 6 / sec 10.B);
4. emit + CACHE LLVM for it keyed by a body fingerprint (doc Layer 6 codegen cache);
5. re-run after a no-op edit; confirm the query + codegen are REUSED (early-cutoff).

DELIVERABLE: the slice runs + produces correct output; baseline numbers recorded (parse/typeck/codegen latency + incremental-rerun latency); a 1-page go/no-go write-up — did the layers compose cleanly? integration surprises? perf within expectations?

FILES: a scratch module under bootstrap/ (NOT wired into the real pipeline). Spine: docs/2026_06_14_AST_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH_EPIC.md.

Replace source_line counter IDs with monotonic IDs per function. Emit a .covmap.json file during compilation that maps each counter_id to:
{
  "counters": [
    {"id": 0, "type": "function_entry", "fn": "main", "line": 10},
    {"id": 1, "type": "branch_then", "fn": "main", "line": 12, "branch": 0},
    {"id": 2, "type": "branch_else", "fn": "main", "line": 12, "branch": 0},
    ...
  ]
}
This decouples counter allocation from line numbers and enables branch tracking.

