Short-circuiting existence check.

```avra
fn Type__any(self: Type, pred: (Type) -> bool) -> bool {
    if pred(self) { return true }
    for c in self.children() {
        if c.any(pred) { return true }
    }
    false
}
```

Simpler than find() — bool return, no nullable. Should land right after visit() with the same decoder coverage.

## Acceptance

- Tree.any(t -> t is .Leaf) on Node(Leaf, Leaf) returns true.
- Tree.any(t -> false) returns false for any tree.

