- y9y4.3 (visit)

Short-circuiting search. Returns the first node matching pred or null.

```avra
fn Type__find(self: Type, pred: (Type) -> bool) -> Type? {
    if pred(self) { return self }
    for c in self.children() {
        let r = c.find(pred)
        if r != null { return r }
    }
    null
}
```

## Why split

visit() returns void. find() returns Type? — nullable return. The macro needs to emit Stmt.Return and check for null. Stmt.Return is decoded; the null check is Expr.Binary with BinOp.BangEqual + Expr.Null. Already covered.

## Acceptance

- Tree.find(t -> t is .Node) on Node(Leaf(1), Leaf(2)) returns Some(Node).
- Pattern.find(p -> p is .LitInt) on NestedVariant("Some", [LitInt(42)]) returns Some(LitInt(42)).

